WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:10.364
This is Osprey Agent on macOS: a real SwiftUI app, with its application logic written in Osprey and compiled ahead of time through LLVM.

00:13.917 --> 00:18.895
Give it a precise task: run the tests, fix the calc package, and leave the tests alone.

00:18.995 --> 00:29.262
Everything here is live. The agent runs the tests, reads the failing code, edits it, and runs the tests again, and each step lands in the conversation as it happens.

00:33.717 --> 00:42.377
Open the activity to check exactly what it ran. The inspector counts requests, tool calls and tokens, and lists every file it changed.

00:52.617 --> 00:59.779
Ask for the code, and it comes back with syntax highlighting, drawn by native controls with no embedded browser engine.

00:59.879 --> 01:10.571
Typed effects keep model requests and tools behind the host boundary. The agent is not sandboxed: it can run any command your account can. Osprey is actively evolving.
